  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Anglican Alliance strategic partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objectives (updated July 2025 based on AA proposal for Year 2 - Jan-Dec 2025)
&#xa0;1)&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0; Protecting the planet and communities living on the front line of climate change. Specifically to support indigenous voices in the climate debate,&#xa0; supporting indigenous theologies and their role in ecumenical and wider public work, seeking to influence narratives around COP30 and COP31.
2)&#xa0;&#xa0; 2. Support Peace building in S Sudan: Specifically to enable Canon Grace Kaiso to continue his work of peace building in South Sudan, working with faith leaders across the region to enable the church to take on more of a leadership role in the country.
3)&#xa0;&#xa0; Gender Justice. Development and testing of a short course on Men and Masculinities, for men to come together and discuss issues of masculinity within cultural contexts. The aim of the course is to transform relationships and end gender-based violence, providing a foundational household base for sustainable development.
4) Reimagining power. Collaboration around the Anglican Alliance plans for strengthening national level advocacy through their &quot;reimagining power&quot; work.</narrative>
  </description>
